      "description": "Watch Chelsea vs Johor Darul Takzim FC highlights and goals from Friendly on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 9, 2026. The friendly encounter between Johor Darul Takzim FC and Chelsea on August 9, 2026, delivered a spectacle that few had anticipated. Both sets of supporters were treated to a match defined by tactical shifts and a relentless pursuit of victory in a high-octane environment. Second Half Intensity and the Penalty Breakthrough After a tightly contested opening period, the game exploded into life during the second half. The referee was kept busy early on, issuing yellow cards to J. Silva and Chelsea's Estêvão as the physical nature of the contest increased. The deadlock in the scoreline was broken in the 62nd minute when Liam Delap stepped up to convert a penalty, giving the visitors a 1-2 lead. However, the lead was short-lived. Just three minutes later, Arribas found the back of the net to bring Johor Darul Takzim FC level at 2-2. The intensity remained high as Nicolas Jackson , A. Cristian , and G. Quenda all entered the book in a frantic ten-minute spell that saw the momentum swing back and forth. A Late Twist at the Death As the match entered its final stages, it appeared that the home side had secured a famous result. In the 86th minute, Bergson struck to make it 3-2, sending the home crowd into raptures. But the drama was far from over. In a cruel twist for the hosts, A. Cristian inadvertently turned the ball into his own net in the 89th minute, handing Chelsea an equalizer. A late yellow card for R. Watson in stoppage time concluded the events, leaving both managers with plenty to reflect on after a thrilling 3-3 draw that showcased the attacking flair of both squads."
